@startuml MenuControllerVersionCOMMAND

class MenuController {

}
CommandInvoker "1" <-down- MenuController: calls

note "The Controller has methods that will call the \nCommandInvoker by creating a new Command, with \nthe information from the request of the REST Endpoints" as N1
N1 -down- MenuController
'Command, CommandInvoker, CommandLog
class CommandInvoker {
    - sessionValidator: SessionValidator
    - commandLogRepo: CommandLogRepository
    + process<T>(command: Command<T>, userSession: Session): CommandSuccess<T>
}
note "process(...) will use the session validator to validate the user's session, \nand check the user's roles against the command's permitted roles, and it will \nlog the result (success or failure) of the command into the command log repository" as N2
N2 -down- CommandInvoker

CommandInvoker .down.> Command : executes
interface Command <<interface>> {
    + {abstract} validRoles(): Set<UserRole>
    + {abstract} execute(): CommandSuccess<T>
}

note left of Command
    - validRoles() will return a set of valid user roles under which
    the command is allowed to execute.
    - execute() delegates the responsibility of the command to MenuService
    and returns CommandSuccess<T>, where T is the response type associated 
    with the concrete command being executed.
end note

MenuController ..> ConcreteCommands : creates
rectangle ConcreteCommands {
    class UpdateItemAvailabilityCommand{
        - session: Session
        - service: MenuService
        - restaurantId: String
        - itemId: String
        - newStatus: MenuItemStatus
        + execute(): CommandSuccess<T>
        + validRoles(): Set<UserRole>
    }

    class AddMenuItemCommand{
        - session: Session
        - service: MenuService
        - restaurantId: String
        - input: MenuItemInput
        + execute(): CommandSuccess<T>
        + validRoles(): Set<UserRole>
    }

    class EditMenuItemCommand {
        - session: Session
        - service: MenuService
        - restaurantId: String
        - itemId: String
        - input: MenuItemInput
        + execute(): CommandSuccess<T>
        + validRoles(): Set<UserRole>
    }

    class RemoveMenuItemCommand {
        - session: Session
        - service: MenuService
        - restaurantId: String
        - itemId: String
        + execute(): CommandSuccess<T>
        + validRoles(): Set<UserRole>
    }

    class BrowseMenuCommand {
        - session: Session
        - menuService: MenuService
        - restaurantId: String
        + execute(): CommandSuccess<T>
        + validRoles(): Set<UserRole>
    }

}

Command <|.. UpdateItemAvailabilityCommand
Command <|.. AddMenuItemCommand
Command <|.. EditMenuItemCommand
Command <|.. RemoveMenuItemCommand
Command <|.. BrowseMenuCommand

MenuService <.up. UpdateItemAvailabilityCommand
MenuService <.up. AddMenuItemCommand
MenuService <.up. EditMenuItemCommand
MenuService <.up. RemoveMenuItemCommand
MenuService <.up. BrowseMenuCommand


class MenuService {
    + updateItemAvailability(userId: String, role: UserRole, restaurantId: String, itemId: String, newStat: MenuItemStatus): MenuItem
    + addMenuItem(userId: String, role: UserRole, restaurantId: String, input: MenuItemInput): MenuItemResponse
    + editMenuItem(userId: String, role: UserRole, restaurantId: String, itemId: String, input: MenuItemInput): MenuItemResponse
    + removeMenuItem(userId: String, role: UserRole, restaurantId: String, itemId: String): MenuItemResponse
    + browseMenu(restaurantId: String, userId: String, role: UserRole): RestaurantMenu
}

@enduml